# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages (see docs/DEPLOY.md). Vite copies this file
# from public/ to the root of dist/.
#
# Pages already sends `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and
# `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, and by default makes the
# browser revalidate every file (`Cache-Control: max-age=0, must-revalidate`). That
# default is exactly right for index.html, sw.js and manifest.webmanifest, so they
# are left alone.
#
# When several rules match one URL, Pages merges their headers and joins repeated
# header names with a comma. So each header name is set in ONE rule only:
# Permissions-Policy in `/*`, Cache-Control in `/assets/*`. A test checks this.

/*
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# Files Vite emits under /assets/ carry a content hash in their name, so they never
# change under the same URL and can be cached for a year.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
